## Develop

Install the tool versions declared by mise.toml / package.json, manually or with `mise install`.
Then run:

```sh
pnpm run bootstrap
pnpm run fmt
pnpm run check
pnpm run build
pnpm run doctor
```

Rendering never installs packages or runs formatters. The explicit first-time `fmt` step
normalizes rendered files. Review and commit the changes and resolver-produced lockfile.
Subsequent CI installations are frozen. No lockfile has been fabricated by the template.

`just` lists command aliases. Use `pnpm run dev` for rebuilding; it does not reload IINA.
For UI presets, build then run `pnpm run preview` for a loopback-only browser simulation.
`pnpm run fixture:media` creates a first-party WAV under ignored reports without playing it.

## Native development and release

On macOS, use `pnpm run link`, `pnpm run unlink` and `pnpm run pack`. Never confuse
`pnpm run pack` with the package manager's own `pnpm pack`. The native IINA CLI is required.
The wrapper never restarts IINA. Python 3 is needed only by development-time ZIP inspection.

The generated CI validates real builds. The release workflow uploads a candidate stage,
not a native-certified plugin and not a public release. After native acceptance, copy the
native evidence example to reports/native-evidence.json, record the exact tested commit,
and run `pnpm run release:prepare` from that clean tagged source. Results are user-reported
native evidence checked for schema and source binding, not native tests executed by that script.

## Documentation

Edit `docs/content`. `pnpm run docs:check` checks local Markdown destinations.
`pnpm run docs:prepare` derives command reference, llms.txt and individual Markdown exports.
[% if docs_profile == 'starlight' %]
Use `pnpm run docs:dev` and `pnpm run docs:build` for Starlight. Configure GitHub Pages
and set the repository variable ENABLE_DOCS_DEPLOY=true to enable the deployment job.
[% endif %]
[% if hooks %]
Lefthook configuration is included but not activated. Install a standalone Lefthook binary,
review existing hooks, then run `pnpm run hooks:install`. Existing hooks are never overwritten.
[% endif %]

Read AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/content/updating.md before changing infrastructure.
Runtime code and user docs are consumer-owned seeds. Copier updates overwrite `site/**`,
so consumer theming there will be replaced on the next reviewed upgrade. Identity in this
template means plugin name, identifier, and Info.json — not the Starlight palette.
Preset/profile changes require a reviewed migration. Renovate may propose updates but no
update is auto-merged.

This project does not inherit a native compatibility certification from its generator.
Record the exact IINA/macOS combinations that you actually test.
